{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And like the sand [your seed].</b> The number of your seed." "<b>And the offspring of your bowels.</b> Like your belly." "<b>Like its bowels.</b> Like the bowels of the sea, and behold he mentioned the waves and the sand, and the word \"like its bowels\" is a hint to the bowels of the fish." "The vav of <b>its name</b> [that is] upon your seed: the vav belongs to <b>שמו</b>, which is upon the seed."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:36.577311707Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}